  "title": "RFK Jr. Brings the “Real Food” Message to the Kitchen",
  "summary": "U.S. Health and Human Services Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. is taking his campaign for a return to whole, minimally processed foods beyond policy announcements and into the kitchen. Through a new government-backed cooking series called The Real Food Show, Kennedy is working with professional chefs to promote affordable meals made with everyday ingredients. The series is part of the Trump administration’s broader “Make America Healthy Again” agenda, which places greater emphasis on nutrition,",
